From 2b892420706ab3c34d6b5139984ac9479da3c29d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:13:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: every lifecycle write on a card under
 another machine's live Board lease is refused before it writes

At 2026-11-13 04:18:25 PST on laptop-1, `hermes kanban complete t_01a1ccfeab615947 --summary ...` printed
`Completed` and exited 0 while worker-6 held the card under its Board lease. The local DB wrote `done`, closed the
run mirror and appended `completed`; the Board then rejected the status (`sync_rejected` live_claim) and the card
read back `running` until worker-6 completed it itself.

Five whys:
1. Why "Completed"? `_cmd_complete` refuses only replica copies (`_foreign_card`) and local live claims
   (`kb.LiveClaimError`).
2. Why no live claim? A remote Board lease is only mirrored (`tasks.lease_holder`/`lease_expires`, `claim_lock`
   NULL), so the local guard never fires.
3. Why did the damage outlast the rejection? The Board fences only the tasks lifecycle columns (status,
   current_run_uid, result, started_at, completed_at). The run update and the `completed` event are unfenced, so
   they were accepted: subscribers got a "done" notice for the rejected write, and the holder's run on the Board
   still carries the rejected summary, metadata and ended_at (run uid 01a1d4d6-c423-..., also two older cards).
4. Why only the CLI? The kanban_* tools already had `_remote_lease_refusal`; the CLI never called
   `kanban_remote_stop.remote_holder()` (only archive did).
5. Fix: check `remote_holder()` before any CLI lifecycle verb runs.

Change:
- `kanban_remote_stop.cli_refusal(action, args)`, called from `kanban_command` before the handler, for complete,
  block, schedule, unblock, request-review, request-changes, reopen-review, reclaim, move, reassign, promote,
  reopen, and edit with --result. A bulk command with one remote-leased id writes nothing. `--force` does not
  bypass it (the Board rejects the write anyway).
- One message for CLI and tools (`kanban_remote_stop.refusal`): `cannot <verb> <id>: it is running under
  <holder>'s live lease. Nothing changed. Let <holder>'s run finish, or archive it to stop it.` Tool errors keep
  `rejection: live_claim`, `code: remote_live_lease`, `holder`.
- kanban_move joins the fenced tools (its creator repin path writes a card it does not run).
- Archive's stop-request route is unchanged.

Proof (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_remote_lease_status_writes.py, two-gateway fake Board):
- RED on base: `complete <id> --summary x` exits 0 and prints `Completed <id>` (assert rc != 0 fails).
- GREEN: every CLI verb above (13) and every lifecycle tool (8) exits non-zero / returns the typed error naming
  the holder, with a byte-for-byte unchanged DB snapshot (tasks, task_runs, task_events, kanban_sync_outbox,
  notify state), no `completed` event, no unseen completion notice for a subscriber, current run's
  status/outcome/summary/metadata/ended_at unchanged, and no `sync_rejected` after a sync round.
- Regressions: expired lease and own-gateway lease still complete; a title edit under a remote lease still works.
- 116 related test files (every test importing the kanban CLI + remote archive/relay suites): 2898 passed.

Follow-ups: dashboard status writes t_01a1d4fa7525888e; one-time Board run-row repair t_01a1d4faf1ecda4b.
Card: t_01a1d4df5b551228.
